    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14406" root="رب" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَرْبُوبٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَبِيبٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also <i>A slave; a bondman;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوكٌ</span> [lit. <i>possessed,</i> and now particularly applied to <i>a male white slave</i>]. (M, K.)
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">العِبَادُ مَرْبُوبُونَ لِلّٰهِ</span> means [<i>Mankind</i> (lit. <i>the servants</i> of God) <i>are</i>] <i>bondmen</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوكُونَ</span>) [<i>to
God</i>]. (M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  A skin for clarified butter &amp;c.
<i>seasoned with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُبّ</span> [or <i>inspissated juice</i>]. (T, S.)
[And A jar <i>smeared</i> with tar or pitch: see 1.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرَبَّبٌ</span>.

